      "text": "Claim: Adding `* text=auto` to .gitattributes and setting `core.autocrlf=false` will prevent recurrence on all platforms. Applicability: This is standard Git behavior; `text=auto` normalizes to LF in the repository and `core.autocrlf=false` prevents automatic CRLF conversion on checkout. Counterexample: If a contributor uses a tool that writes CRLF regardless of Git settings (e.g., some Windows editors), the file can still be committed with CRLF if the file is re-added; a pre-commit hook is the only enforcement that catches this. Therefore, the fix must include both .gitattributes and a pre-commit/CI check.",
      "layer": "L3",
      "confidence": 0.90
